# MANUAL SPEC MUTANT r4-a06-size-pickers/01
# type: ComplexTestStruct
# ops: encode
# spec: the size of a byte list / packed basic list is its byte length n; the object is not valid when its storage does not hold ceil(n / 4) words, and nothing that large may be allocated
# fault: the storage test counts floor(n / 4) words (n + 3 dropped): a length whose last partial word is not stored is sized as valid
# why: ceil vs floor
# file: src/obj.bend
# sym: wsz_pick,words_sizek
--- a/src/obj.bend
+++ b/src/obj.bend
@@ -1800,3 +1800,3 @@
   (ws, +c) = pair
-  (Words{ws, n}, pick(U32.is_le(U32.shrn((n + 3 : U32), 2n), c), n, 4294967295))
+  (Words{ws, n}, pick(U32.is_le(U32.shrn(n, 2n), c), n, 4294967295))
 
